MySQL EXAM — KEYS & JOINS
Topic Coverage
Keys: Primary Key, Foreign Key, Candidate Key, Alternate Key, Super Key, Composite Key, Unique Key, Natural vs Surrogate Key
Joins: INNER, LEFT, RIGHT, CROSS, SELF, multi-table JOINs, JOIN conditions, unmatched records, practical scenarios

Exam rule: Don't memorize JOIN syntax. For every JOIN question, first identify what data you need, from which tables, and what should happen to unmatched rows

SECTION A — MCQs
1. Which key uniquely identifies each row in a table?
A. Foreign Key
B. Primary Key
C. Alternate Key
D. Super Key -- B

2. Which statement about a primary key is correct?
A. A table can have multiple primary key constraints
B. Primary key values can be duplicated
C. Primary key uniquely identifies rows
D. Primary key is always a foreign key -- C

3. Which key establishes a relationship between two tables?
A. Candidate Key
B. Foreign Key
C. Alternate Key
D. Composite Key -- B

4. Which is an example of a composite key?
A. customer_id
B. email
C. (order_id, product_id)
D. phone  -- C (Two columns together uniquely identify the row)

5. A candidate key that is not selected as the primary key is called:
A. Foreign Key
B. Alternate Key
C. Super Key
D. Composite Key -- B

6. Which JOIN returns only matching records from both tables?
A. LEFT JOIN
B. RIGHT JOIN
C. INNER JOIN
D. CROSS JOIN -- C

7. Which JOIN returns all rows from the left table and matching rows from the right table?
A. INNER JOIN
B. LEFT JOIN
C. RIGHT JOIN
D. CROSS JOIN -- D(Every row combines with every other row)

8. What does a CROSS JOIN produce?
A. Only matching rows
B. Only unmatched rows
C. Cartesian product
D. Duplicate elimination

9. Which JOIN is useful when you want:
"All customers, including customers who have never placed an order"
A. INNER JOIN
B. LEFT JOIN
C. CROSS JOIN
D. SELF JOIN -- B (Keeps all customers, even without orders)

10. MySQL does not provide a direct:
A. INNER JOIN
B. LEFT JOIN
C. RIGHT JOIN
D. FULL OUTER JOIN -- D (MySQL has no direct FULL OUTER JOIN)

SECTION B — TRUE / FALSE
11. A table can have only one primary key constraint -- True
12. A foreign key must always be unique -- False
13. A composite key consists of two or more columns  -- True
14. INNER JOIN can return unmatched rows from the left table -- False
15. LEFT JOIN can return NULL values for columns from the right table when no match exists -- True

